# Custom Odoo modules

Create a new module with the Odoo scaffold, not by hand:

```bash
docker compose run --rm odoo odoo scaffold hp_example /mnt/extra-addons
```

Conventions:

- Module technical name: `hp_` prefix, lowercase, underscores.
- Every module has `__manifest__.py` with `name`, `version`, `depends`, `license`, and `data` listing its XML files.
- Depend only on Odoo Community modules in `depends`.
- Extend core views with `inherit_id` and `xpath`. Never edit core files.
- Use `_()` around user-facing strings.
- Give access rights in `security/ir.model.access.csv`. Add record rules when needed.
- Add tests under `tests/` using Odoo's test framework (`TransactionCase`).

Example: extend the partner form.

```xml
<record id="view_partner_form_hp" model="ir.ui.view">
    <field name="name">res.partner.form.hp</field>
    <field name="model">res.partner</field>
    <field name="inherit_id" ref="base.view_partner_form"/>
    <field name="arch" type="xml">
        <xpath expr="//field[@name='vat']" position="after">
            <field name="hp_reference"/>
        </xpath>
    </field>
</record>
```

After changing a module, follow the upgrade steps in `local-odoo.mdc`.
